  "notes": "Swedish shout-pop duo over electro/indie-dance production. The defining parameter the entry names is the vocal: \"the shouted, unison two-voice topline — no harmony, no melisma, both voices doubling the same line at the top of their range as a chant\". That is a high, narrow, stepwise, staccato melody with almost no octave jump and a deliberately thin countermelody, because there is no harmony part to give it. The electro-house lineage supplies the kit — \"hard-clipped four-square kick, distorted layered clap on 2&4, and 16th hats; fills are white-noise sweeps\" — so the perc lanes are riser/impact/snap rather than a hand-percussion bed, the snare-roll ladder is off, and the clap offset is the widest here at 4-10 ms for the smeared, distorted layer. The bass is the documented electro-house convention, \"buzzing sawtooth-and-distortion locked to the kick and sidechained hard\": a kick mirror at 0.95 roots. Harmony is \"deliberately blunt\", two- or four-chord majors. ⚠ The research marks the tonality claim `[LOW-CONF]` and calls the drum and bass parameters convention-derived; both marks are repeated here, and every velocity, density and probability above is INFERRED.",
